    {
      "content": "By Matthew Choi",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "type": "byline",
      "authors": [
        {
          "id": "choim",
          "url": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/people/matthew-choi/",
          "name": "Matthew Choi",
          "bio": "Matthew Choi covers politics for The Washington Post. He previously covered Washington for The Texas Tribune and energy for Politico.",
          "expertise": "Congress, campaigns, politics",
          "image": "https://author-service-images-prod-us-east-1.publishing.aws.arc.pub/washpost/fde52f99-c7c8-434b-9adb-f4a249c7b8a6.png"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "arcId": "F5YBQU7HXND3XB4VDBOTVRZMTM",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "South Dakota Gov. Larry Rhoden staved off a grassroots challenge Tuesday, defeating businessman Toby Doeden in a competitive Republican primary."
    },
    {
      "arcId": "2DHNDVBBJFBCFKIHYRDGV4A26Y",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "Rhoden, a former lieutenant governor, became governor in 2025 after his predecessor Kristi L. Noem left office to become President Donald Trump’s Homeland Security<b> </b>secretary. But despite his incumbent advantage, he came in second place in the June primary with about 25 percent of the vote."
    },
    {
      "arcId": "EQKQNLTXEJDNFAPXLX2YHFQFMQ",
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "Doeden, who once <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0PLe-zbgYSE\">described himself</a> as being “probably the least political person you had ever met” before his campaign, finished first in June with about 31 percent of the vote. He spent more than $4 million of his own money on the campaign and cast himself as a political outsider."
    },
    {
      "type": "web_embed",
      "hideUntilReady": false,
      "url": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/partials/elections/iframes/sd-governor-runoff.html",
      "subtype": "partial",
      "widthFactor": "default"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad",
      "breakpoints": [
        "small"
      ],
